    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12404878/comment/12633460",
          "id": "12633460",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mkwhitacre",
            "name": "mkwhitacre",
            "key": "mkwhitacre",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Micah Whitacre",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Chicago"
          },
          "body": "What made you pick version 1.5.2 when version 1.5.3 is available?  I've tested my assemblies using 1.5-SNAPSHOTs with the 1.5.3 versions of slf4j* endstates and did not receive any errors.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mkwhitacre",
            "name": "mkwhitacre",
            "key": "mkwhitacre",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Micah Whitacre",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Chicago"
          },
          "created": "2008-09-22T20:01:39.471+0000",
          "updated": "2008-09-22T20:01:39.471+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12404878/comment/12633478",
          "id": "12633478",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=kalished",
            "name": "kalished",
            "key": "kalished",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stephane Landelle",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I just hadn't noticed that a new release was made 10 days ago. So 1.5.3 it\nis! :)\n\nIf you have a look at the jcl104-over-slf4j\nPOM<http://svn.slf4j.org/viewvc/slf4j/trunk/jcl104-over-slf4j/pom.xml?view=markup>,\nyou'll see that it's deprecated and relocated to jcl-over-slf4j. So it would\nbe cleaner to update the dependency and not only the version.\n\nSincerely,\n\nStephane\n\n\n2008/9/22 Micah Whitacre (JIRA) <jira@apache.org>\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=kalished",
            "name": "kalished",
            "key": "kalished",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stephane Landelle",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2008-09-22T20:25:45.849+0000",
          "updated": "2008-09-22T20:25:45.849+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12404878/comment/12633783",
          "id": "12633783",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "I'm wondering if a better solution would be *not* to use jcl-over-slf4j at all in Jackrabbit, i.e. leave it up to the client application to exclude the transitive commons-logging dependency with jcl-over-slf4j they want.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2008-09-23T16:15:46.829+0000",
          "updated": "2008-09-23T16:15:46.829+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12404878/comment/12633796",
          "id": "12633796",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=kalished",
            "name": "kalished",
            "key": "kalished",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stephane Landelle",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I agree, jackrabbit shouldn't in any way depend on jcl104-over-slf4j with a\ncompile scope.\n\nCurrently, only jackrabbit-webapp and jackrabbit-text-extractor depend on\njcl104-over-slf4j (both with compile scope).\n\nConcerning jackrabbit-webapp, scope should be runtime, not compile as it is\nnow.\nConcerning jackrabbit-text-extractor, I don't understand why it depends on\njcl104-over-slf4j in the first place. Should it be remove? Should scope be\nchanged to test?\n\nSincerely,\n\nStephane Landelle\n\n2008/9/23 Jukka Zitting (JIRA) <jira@apache.org>\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=kalished",
            "name": "kalished",
            "key": "kalished",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stephane Landelle",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2008-09-23T16:41:46.986+0000",
          "updated": "2008-09-23T16:41:46.986+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12404878/comment/12633798",
          "id": "12633798",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Updated the SLF4J dependencies to 1.5.3 in revision 698222.\n\nI reopened the JCR-1631 issue that introduced the jcl104-over-slf4j dependency to text-extractors. The rationale was to replace the transitive commons-logging dependency of Apache POI with SLF4J.",
